# Phase 006 Group 02 — structural compatibility

Status: **Accepted — HLTH-009–HLTH-018; H02-01–H02-30 pass.**

Preserve:

- physical producer schema ≠ consumer-visible interface schema;
- schema snapshot/DDL diff ≠ compatibility by itself;
- declared/governed schema meaning ≠ structural Expectation ≠ proposed state ≠ realized Observation/Change ≠ compatibility Assessment;
- add/drop/rename/reorder/type/precision/nullability/default/generated/key/grain/nested changes remain separately representable;
- rename ≠ drop+add coincidence;
- same field name ≠ guaranteed same semantic identity;
- additive ≠ universally compatible;
- removal ≠ universally breaking;
- reorder matters only for order-sensitive contracts;
- engine cast/parse support ≠ consumer compatibility;
- widening/narrowing compatibility is directional and contract-specific;
- zero observed nulls ≠ preserved NOT NULL guarantee;
- default/generated presence ≠ business completeness/validity;
- key/grain change can be material with no column/type change;
- declared key role ≠ observed uniqueness/non-null/reference quality;
- compatibility is consumer/interface/version/time scoped;
- compatibility is not automatically transitive through Lineage or interfaces;
- stable view/projection can preserve consumer contract despite backing-table DDL change;
- unchanged producer schema can become incompatible if consumer contract changes;
- prospective/pre-deployment validation ≠ realized production validation;
- validated proposal ≠ deployed/realized schema;
- structural change triggers scoped metric/Profile/Baseline review, not global reset;
- structural compatibility ≠ statistical/Baseline comparability;
- `compatible` requires sufficient coverage of all applicable required predicates in scope;
- missing/partial schema evidence ≠ compatible;
- structural incompatibility ≠ job failure ≠ exposure ≠ Impact ≠ cause;
- physical layout/clustering/optimization ≠ logical schema incompatibility unless the relevant contract depends on it;
- validation location remains architecture-neutral in Phase 006.

Group 03 inherits the exact structural/version/grain/interface history and decides empirical Baseline/statistical comparability. Group 04 later decides warning/failure/waiver Assessment composition. Group 05 later decides transformation-aware reconciliation/propagation.
